{
  "schema": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Lambo PHP download catalogue.",
    "",
    "This file is data, not code. It ships inside the binary so that",
    "`lambo php list` works without network access, and it can be overridden",
    "per family by dropping a file of the same shape into",
    "$LAMBO_HOME/config/catalogs/ (php.json, apache.json, mariadb.json,",
    "mysql.json, dbui.json). Entries there replace the ones below when",
    "version and platform match, which is how a stale URL or a corporate",
    "mirror is fixed without waiting for a Lambo release.",
    "",
    "Checksums: `sha256` is optional. When it is null the downloader fetches",
    "the upstream `<url>.sha256` sidecar and verifies against that; when",
    "neither is available the download is refused. Nothing is ever extracted",
    "or executed before it has been verified.",
    "",
    "What is pinned below was pinned from the publisher's own checksum",
    "documents on 2026-09-20: windows.php.net sidecars for PHP, the signed",
    "sha256sums.txt files on archive.mariadb.org for MariaDB, the sidecar on",
    "files.phpmyadmin.net for phpMyAdmin, and the checksum file Apache Lounge",
    "publishes next to each httpd build. Entries left at null have no digest",
    "their publisher exposes in a usable form; they verify through the",
    "sidecar rule above, or fail closed until a digest is pinned here or in",
    "an override file. The dashboard panel keeps its own component table and",
    "resolves the newest Apache Lounge build dynamically.",
    "",
    "Windows Apache note: the Apache HTTP Server project distributes source",
    "code only; the win64 binaries are Apache Lounge builds, so that is what",
    "this entry points at. The URL embeds the build date, which keeps it",
    "stable for this pinned version.",
    "",
    "Platform keys are <os>-<arch>: windows-x64, linux-x64, linux-arm64,",
    "macos-x64, macos-arm64. See docs/installation.md."
  ],
